M50 is accepted as certified complete.
The closure establishes the intended authority model: historical canonical and memory records remain preserved, while every identified active production consumer is governed by current Genesis policy. Policy-drift material is suppressed at consumption rather than deleted, and unavailable/invalid governance fails closed. The Builder's successful authoritative Runtime [] behavior is also now certified rather than being replaced by synthetic state.
The terminal evidence confirms the final Phase 49 prerequisite was committed and synchronized at 823a5c2043fef9dbe42bb3c54683f434226b47a0, with focused tests passing and only the known operational Runtime paths remaining untracked. Phase 50 itself requires no source change.
We should not invent the next milestone from M50. The next bounded objective should be selected from the existing KoreLumina roadmap and current certified implementation state, exactly as we did after M49.
Next instruction

Post-M50 Roadmap Position Audit
Inspect the repository directly at the current source HEAD.
Reconcile:


the current certified implementation state;


CA-005 Learning Constitution;


Vision 2050;


the authoritative implementation roadmap/backlog;


